# KNOWN GAP (`todo/t0877`, arms (c) and (d)) — SELF-HOST lane. Two more body
# shapes the self-host's `guess_return_type` has no arm for, so a
# `String`-returning closure is emitted `int64_t`-returning and the C build
# fails:
#
#     error: incompatible types when returning type 'Str' but 'int64_t' was expected
#
# THE TWO NEW ARMS (`tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/lower_closures.gg`):
#
#   (c) a bare LOCAL identifier body — `(): s`, where `s` is an outer LOCAL
#       rather than a closure parameter. `guess_return_type` DOES have an
#       `EIdentifier` arm, and it consults `gmod.fn_sigs` and nothing else, so
#       it is INERT for a bare local or a closure parameter: the lookup fails,
#       control falls off the arm, and the function reaches its `I64_TYPE`
#       default. Arm (b) of the item names the closure-PARAMETER spelling and
#       diagnoses it correctly; this local spelling fails through the SAME
#       inert arm, so the subject is any bare identifier `fn_sigs` misses.
#       ⚠ An inert arm and an absent arm emit identical C — read the source
#       (`grep -n 'case EIdentifier(name):' \
#       tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/lower_closures.gg`) before claiming
#       either.
#
#   (d) a METHOD-CHAIN body whose result is a `String` — `(): v.get(0).unwrap()`
#       over a `Vector[String]`. The `EMethodCall` arm does not carry the
#       element type back out of the collection, so the chain types `int64_t`.
#
# ⚠ THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE BODY SHAPE, NOT THE RETURN TYPE. A `String`-
# returning closure whose body is a plain CALL — `(): mk(p, "lo")` — compiles
# and runs correctly on the self-host, because the `ECall` arm reads `fn_sigs`.
# That control is why this is `guess_return_type` and not the `Callable[…]`
# annotation being lost.
#
# Rust gg compiles and runs this correctly on C and LLVM, so it is a self-host
# lag — fix the self-host, do not dumb the shape down.
#
# BLAST RADIUS, measured 2026-09-04: three top-level fixtures cannot run on the
# self-host lane for this reason —
# `closure_capture_then_mutate_source_uaf.gg` (arm d),
# `closure_capture_string_then_reassign_source.gg` (arm c),
# `closure_capture_param_bare_identifier_body.gg` (arm b).
# All three are capture-ownership regression cells whose body shape is the
# thing under test, so none of them can be respelled around this.
#
# INTENDED, on the SELF-HOST lane: prints `hello` then `world`, rc 0.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s = mk("hel", "lo")
    Callable[String()] f = (): s
    print(f())

    Vector[String] v = [mk("wor", "ld")]
    Callable[String()] g = (): v.get(0).unwrap()
    print(g())
